{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"**Borrower/default risk:** The borrower may fail to return securities. In the U.S. iShares lending example, the lending agent (an affiliate of BlackRock) arranges loans and requires collateral; this does not guarantee recovery or make losses impossible. Controls include borrower eligibility and limits, collateral haircuts, daily monitoring, and recall rights.\n\n**Collateral-shortfall risk:** If collateral value falls below the replacement cost of loaned securities, the fund may incur a loss, especially during market stress or delayed liquidation. Controls include overcollateralization, frequent marking to market, margin calls, and diversification.\n\n**Cash-reinvestment risk:** Cash collateral invested in securities or other instruments can lose value or become illiquid; that loss can exceed income earned. Controls include investment guidelines, liquidity limits, and maturity/credit limits.\n\n**UCITS rules are separate:** UCITS funds generally must be able to recall lent securities or terminate the lending arrangement at any time. Non-cash collateral must meet applicable eligibility, valuation, haircut, diversification, and custody requirements. These protections mitigate risk; they do not eliminate it."}}
